{"uncertainty": 0.15, "outcome": "rtl_bug", "artifacts": [{"kind": "root_cause_analysis", "title": "Root cause: debounce restarts its stability count only on a rising edge of noisy", "summary": "Requirement [requirement:req-19189b08df]. Inputs: the approved RTL [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1], the triage classification [evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e1] (run [run:run-0001], unknown_failure at 30% confidence, top hypothesis 'Likely RTL bug', which I treated as one candidate among several) and the triage reproduction [evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e2] (run [run:run-0002], 1 of 1 checks failed, $finish at 175000).\n\nCONCLUSION: rtl_bug.\n\nDEFECT: the count-restart condition is `if (noisy && !prev) cnt <= 4'd0;`. This fires only on a rising change of noisy. The header comment of [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1] says the opposite: 'A change on noisy, in either direction, restarts the count, so a pulse of STABLE edges or fewer, high or low, never reaches clean'. That gap is the incorrectness. The restart should fire on `noisy != prev`.\n\nCAUSALITY: suppose noisy has been high long enough that clean=1. Then cnt has saturated at STABLE-1 (3). When noisy falls, the first posedge sees noisy=0 and prev=1. The restart does not fire, and cnt holds at 3 because it is saturated. On the next posedge noisy equals prev (both 0) and cnt equals 3, so clean takes 0. The fault, a stale saturated cnt, is created at the falling edge. It becomes a visible failure one edge later. As a result, a low glitch of 2 edges, well under STABLE=4, reaches clean. This is the behaviour the specification forbids. A rising glitch while clean=0 is filtered correctly, because the rising edge does restart the count.\n\nHYPOTHESES, RANKED, WITH WHAT WOULD REFUTE EACH:\n(1) rtl_bug (accepted). Refuted if a falling glitch of at most STABLE edges left clean unchanged on this RTL. The cycle trace above shows that it does not.\n(2) testbench_bug (rejected). Refuted when the expected value, re-derived from the RTL's own specification comment, matches the check. It does: clean must not follow a short low pulse. The new repro takes its expectations only from that comment, not from the RTL's outputs.\n(3) infrastructure (rejected, with less certainty). Refuted if the failure is deterministic and explained by the RTL logic. [evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e2] reports a clean build and a reached $finish with one failed check, and the RTL logic alone explains that failure. I have no clean-rebuild run to cite.\n(4) spec_ambiguity (rejected). Refuted when the clause the check relies on fixes the behaviour. The comment explicitly says 'either direction' and 'high or low'.\n\nThe repro testbench is debounce_fall_glitch_repro.v, which the platform gates against [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1]."}], "files": [{"path": "debounce_fall_glitch_repro.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking repro: a short low glitch must not reach clean", "summary": "Minimal self-checking repro for [requirement:req-19189b08df] against [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1]. The testbench resets the design, then holds noisy high for 20 cycles and checks that clean=1. It then drops noisy low for 2 clock edges (under STABLE=4), samples clean every cycle and checks that it never fell. Next it holds noisy low for 20 cycles and checks that clean=0. Finally it applies a 2-edge high glitch and checks that clean stays 0. All expectations come from the specification comment. I expect the second check to fail on the RTL under investigation and all four to pass on a design that restarts on any change. The testbench reads nirmaan_nonce and prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict just before $finish.", "entry": "tb_debounce_fall_glitch"}], "tool_runs": ["run-0001", "run-0002"], "claims": ["By cycle analysis, I expect the new repro to report 1 failed check (the low-glitch check) on debounce_rise_only_restart.v.", "I expect the new repro to pass all 4 checks on a debouncer that restarts its count on any change of noisy (noisy != prev).", "Infrastructure is rejected by reasoning from a deterministic, logic-explained failure; no clean-rebuild experiment is available to cite."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Independent review is still required and is not claimed here. The reproduction gate (simulator.run, expect=fail) is the platform's to run over debounce_fall_glitch_repro.v. The suggested fix is to replace `if (noisy && !prev)` with `if (noisy != prev)`. After that fix, look for the same edge-direction asymmetry in other debouncer or synchronizer blocks, and consider adding an assertion that clean changes only after noisy has been stable for STABLE edges."}
=== FILE: debounce_fall_glitch_repro.v ===
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
// Repro: per the debounce specification, a pulse of STABLE edges or fewer,
// high or low, never reaches `clean`. This bench drives a 2-edge low glitch
// while clean is high and a 2-edge high glitch while clean is low.
module tb_debounce_fall_glitch;
    reg clk   = 1'b0;
    reg rst   = 1'b1;
    reg noisy = 1'b0;
    wire clean;

    integer passed = 0;
    integer failed = 0;
    integer i;
    reg     changed;
    reg [8*64-1:0] nonce;

    debounce #(.STABLE(4)) dut (
        .clk  (clk),
        .rst  (rst),
        .noisy(noisy),
        .clean(clean)
    );

    always #5 clk = ~clk;

    initial begin
        if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce))
            nonce = "none";

        // Reset
        rst   = 1'b1;
        noisy = 1'b0;
        repeat (3) @(negedge clk);
        rst = 1'b0;
        repeat (3) @(negedge clk);

        // Check 1: a long high hold reaches clean.
        noisy = 1'b1;
        repeat (20) @(negedge clk);
        if (clean === 1'b1) passed = passed + 1;
        else begin
            failed = failed + 1;
            $display("FAIL check1: clean=%b after long high hold, expected 1", clean);
        end

        // Check 2: a 2-edge low glitch must not reach clean.
        changed = 1'b0;
        noisy = 1'b0;
        for (i = 0; i < 2; i = i + 1) begin
            @(negedge clk);
            if (clean !== 1'b1) changed = 1'b1;
        end
        noisy = 1'b1;
        for (i = 0; i < 12; i = i + 1) begin
            @(negedge clk);
            if (clean !== 1'b1) changed = 1'b1;
        end
        if (!changed) passed = passed + 1;
        else begin
            failed = failed + 1;
            $display("FAIL check2: 2-edge low glitch reached clean (STABLE=4)");
        end

        // Check 3: a long low hold reaches clean.
        noisy = 1'b0;
        repeat (20) @(negedge clk);
        if (clean === 1'b0) passed = passed + 1;
        else begin
            failed = failed + 1;
            $display("FAIL check3: clean=%b after long low hold, expected 0", clean);
        end

        // Check 4: a 2-edge high glitch must not reach clean.
        changed = 1'b0;
        noisy = 1'b1;
        for (i = 0; i < 2; i = i + 1) begin
            @(negedge clk);
            if (clean !== 1'b0) changed = 1'b1;
        end
        noisy = 1'b0;
        for (i = 0; i < 12; i = i + 1) begin
            @(negedge clk);
            if (clean !== 1'b0) changed = 1'b1;
        end
        if (!changed) passed = passed + 1;
        else begin
            failed = failed + 1;
            $display("FAIL check4: 2-edge high glitch reached clean (STABLE=4)");
        end

        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
        $finish;
    end
endmodule
=== END FILE ===
